  "notes": "Both charts transcribed from the OEM 'Mini Gobo Moving head Light' manual PDF hosted by Amazon (Lixada listing, 81ej8MIZpBL.pdf) and cross-checked against the Open Fixture Library Lixada definition, which is the same 9/11ch layout; ZKYMZL's own manuals.plus page confirms 9/11CH, 8 colours, 8 gobos, pan 570 / tilt 270 (ZKYMZL says 570/270, the OEM manual says 540/180 -- 540/180 kept), 3.2 kg, box 33x22x23 cm. Beam angle: OEM manual says 11 deg; Amazon TY-30 listing says 30 deg (almost certainly wrong); the caller expected ~15 deg -- 11 deg used, flagged as guess. Size 280x210x260 mm (LxWxH) and 3.4 kg from the OEM manual; ZKYMZL says 3.2 kg / 2.54 kg on Amazon. Colour order (red, pale-blue, orange, blue, yellow, green, pink) comes from the OFL definition (community-entered), the manual only says '8 colours'; U'King ZQ02061 listing lists red, yellow, blue, green, pink, orange + white. Gobo slot DMX positions are not itemised by the manual (0-63 select, ~8 values each). The 9ch mode has NO fine channels: Pan, Tilt, Color, Gobo, Strobe, Dimmer, Speed, Function, DimmerCurve. CONFLICTS with the repo's venue-console 11ch map: attribute order matches exactly (Pan, PanFine, Tilt, TiltFine, Color, Gobo, Shutter, Dimmer, Speed, Function, Dimmer Modes) but the repo guessed 8 colours in 8-value steps -- the real colour wheel uses 16-value steps (0-15 white ... 112-127 pink) with rotation above 128, and the repo's colour order (White, Red, Green, Blue, Yellow, Magenta, Cyan, Orange) does not match the OFL order. Repo already has GDTFs Lixada@Mini_Gobo_Moving_Head and UKing_old@Mini_Gobo_Moving_Head_2022 for this OEM. manuals.plus and device.report block automated fetches (HTTP 403 / JS challenge) so ZKYMZL's own chart was not read directly."
